BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-13@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
SUMMARY:Easy Endurance — 14 km
DESCRIPTION:14 km genuinely easy and mostly flat\; no strides\, hills\, fast finish\, or pace objective.\nPace: 4:40–5:20/km or slower by feel\; keep breathing clearly easy.\nHR: Use HR only as a cap/secondary check.\nRecovery: No structured recovery.\nTerrain: Flat to gently rolling\, under 150 m ascent.\nPurpose: Retain running endurance 14 days before the HM without turning a tired-quads day into another stimulus.\nIf fatigued: Reduce to 8–10 km or rest if stiffness changes mechanics\, pain is focal\, or the stride does not loosen after 10 minutes.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,EASY ENDURANCE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-14@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Rest — 0 km
DESCRIPTION:Full non-running day. Optional easy walk and 10–15 min mobility.\nPace: None.\nHR: None.\nRecovery: Full recovery day.\nTerrain: Flat/none.\nPurpose: Absorb the previous week\, keep six run days sustainable\, and arrive fresh for Tuesday quality.\nIf fatigued: Keep the rest day\; do not replace missed mileage here.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,REST
STATUS:CONFIRMED
