BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-15@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Hm-Specific Primer — 11 km
DESCRIPTION:3 km easy\; drills + 4 strides\; 2 × 2 km at controlled HM effort with 1 km easy jog\; 3 km cool-down.\nPace: 3:33–3:35/km. This is a rhythm check after Friday's 4 × 2 km session\, not a test or a substitute for missed 2 × 5 km work.\nHR: Let HR rise naturally\; stop after one rep if the warm-up or first block feels laboured.\nRecovery: 1 km genuinely easy jog between the 2 km blocks.\nTerrain: Flat\, accurately measured route with minimal interruptions.\nPurpose: Re-establish goal-HM rhythm before the Night Run without stacking a second maximal session.\nIf fatigued: Use 1 × 2 km at HM effort\, or run 8–10 km easy\, if legs remain loaded.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,HM-SPECIFIC PRIMER
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-16@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Recovery — 7 km
DESCRIPTION:7 km very easy\, flat recovery\; no strides.\nPace: 4:50–5:30/km or slower by feel.\nHR: Use HR only as a cap/secondary check.\nRecovery: No structured recovery.\nTerrain: Flat/gentle\; avoid hard descents.\nPurpose: Arrive fresh for Thursday rather than accumulating mileage.\nIf fatigued: Rest if legs are not springy.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,RECOVERY
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-17@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
SUMMARY:Vienna Night Run — Controlled 5 Km B-Race — 9 km
DESCRIPTION:2 km warm-up\; drills + 4 strides\; 5 km Vienna Night Run\; 2 km cool-down if convenient. Run it progressively: first km 3:25–3:27/km\, km 2–4 at 3:20–3:22/km\, then hold form through the final km without a finishing sprint.\nPace: Target 16:40–16:55: approximately 97–98% effort\, hard but below an all-out PB attempt.\nHR: Race HR is observational only. Control the first kilometre\; effort is about 9/10\, not a final-kilometre sprint.\nRecovery: No interval recovery. Rehydrate and refuel after the evening event.\nTerrain: Vienna Ringstraße 5 km circuit\; allow for start congestion and bends.\nPurpose: A sanctioned sharpening stimulus that replaces the planned 400 m economy session.\nIf fatigued: If Tuesday was laboured or legs remain heavy\, run 17:05–17:15 with no final-kilometre push\, or jog the event socially.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,VIENNA NIGHT RUN — CONTROLLED 5 KM B-RACE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
