BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-25@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:Easy + Strides — 6 km
DESCRIPTION:6 km easy\, then 6 × 15–20 s relaxed strides on flat ground with full recovery.\nPace: Easy running 4:30–5:10/km by feel\; strides fast but relaxed\, never sprinting.\nHR: Use HR as a cap/secondary check\, not a target. No threshold inference from HR alone.\nRecovery: 60–90 s walk/jog after each stride.\nTerrain: Flat to gently rolling\; save climbing and faster aerobic work for the planned weekend session.\nPurpose: Neuromuscular freshness without becoming a third metabolic workout.\nIf fatigued: Omit the strides and run 7–9 km easy\, or rest if recovery is poor.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,EASY + STRIDES
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-26@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Shakeout — 5 km
DESCRIPTION:5 km very easy + 4 × 10–12 s relaxed strides if desired.\nPace: No pace target\; finish fresher than you started.\nHR: Use HR as a cap/secondary check\, not a target. No threshold inference from HR alone.\nRecovery: Full walk/jog recovery after optional strides.\nTerrain: Flat/gentle\; avoid technical descents.\nPurpose: Stay loose without adding fatigue before race day.\nIf fatigued: Rest instead if soreness changes mechanics or pain is focal/worsening.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,SHAKEOUT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bad-ischl-2026-09-27@local-running-coach
DTSTAMP:20260912T180132Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
SUMMARY:Race — 25.1 km
DESCRIPTION:Race day: 3 km warm-up + drills/strides\, Bad Ischl HM\, 1 km cool-down only if desired.\nPace: Goal pace ~3:33/km. Open controlled\; pace by effort on hills/wind and avoid banking time early.\nHR: HR is observational\, not a pacing target. Use chest strap if comfortable\; ignore anomalous values.\nRecovery: No interval recovery. Fuel/hydrate according to rehearsed practice.\nTerrain: Bad Ischl HM course\; arrive familiar with turns and gradients.\nPurpose: Execute the primary race after a progressive\, intensity-preserving taper.\nIf fatigued: If illness\, focal pain\, or medical concern is present\, do not force the start.
CATEGORIES:RUNNING,RACE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
